# 21. Public CV Privacy Review

Review the CV itself.

The recruiter/public version of the CV should not unnecessarily contain highly sensitive personal information.

Flag or remove where applicable:

- IC number
- Passport number
- Full residential address
- Date of birth
- Banking information
- Personal signature
- Unnecessary personal identifiers
- References' private contact information

Professional contact information may remain where intentionally provided.

Do not automatically remove ambiguous information from the CV. Report questionable fields for review first.

