# 22. Email Endpoint Security

Review the existing email implementation.

Ensure:

- Recipient email addresses are validated.
- User-controlled input cannot manipulate email headers.
- Sender/from address is fixed server-side.
- Email subject is fixed or safely constructed.
- Requesters cannot provide arbitrary email bodies.
- Email API credentials remain server-side.
- Provider errors are not returned directly to users.
- Secrets are never exposed in frontend bundles.

The CV functionality must never become a generic email relay.

