# 23. Prevent Token Leakage

Sensitive tokens can accidentally leak through:

- Browser history
- Server logs
- Analytics
- Referrer headers
- Third-party scripts
- Error-reporting systems

For verification/download routes, consider:

```http
Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
```

Avoid loading unnecessary third-party analytics or resources on token-bearing URLs.

Do not intentionally send token query parameters to analytics platforms.

Where practical, after successful validation:

```text
Token URL
   ↓
Backend validates token
   ↓
Create temporary authorised state/session
   ↓
Redirect to clean URL
```

This prevents the security token from remaining unnecessarily visible in the address bar.

