# 28. Secrets Management

Search the repository for potentially exposed secrets.

Examples:

```text
API_KEY
SECRET
TOKEN
PASSWORD
PRIVATE_KEY
DATABASE_URL
SMTP_PASSWORD
FIREBASE_*
TURNSTILE_SECRET
```

Determine whether each value is intended to be public.

Client-side Firebase configuration should not automatically be treated as a secret, but the corresponding Firebase security rules must be reviewed.

Sensitive credentials must be moved to the appropriate server-side secret/environment configuration.

If an actual secret has previously been committed to Git, removing it from the latest file is insufficient.

The credential should also be **rotated**.

