# 33. Security Philosophy

The portfolio should remain open enough to demonstrate professional credibility while avoiding unnecessary personal exposure.

The guiding principles are:

> **Publish professional value, not unnecessary identity data.**

> **Verify ownership before granting private resources.**

> **Never trust security controls implemented only in the browser.**

> **Use short-lived, cryptographically secure credentials for temporary access.**

> **A secret URL is not access control.**

> **Collect only the data that has a genuine purpose.**

> **Security should increase attacker friction without unnecessarily increasing recruiter friction.**

